@startuml Preciazo_Identity_Access_Classes
title Preciazo - Identity and Access Domain (AV2 - US06 / TS01)
set namespaceSeparator none
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
class User <<Aggregate>> {
 -id: Long
 -email: EmailAddress
 -passwordHash: PasswordHash
 -status: AccountStatus
 -failedAttempts: Integer
 -lockedUntil: Instant [0..1]
 -securityCheckRequired: Boolean
 -version: Long
 +recordFailedSignIn(now: Instant, policy: AccountLockoutPolicy): void
 +beginPostLockWindow(now: Instant): void
 +acceptSignIn(): void
 +hasPermission(resource: String, action: String): Boolean
}
class EmailAddress <<Value Object>> {
 -canonicalValue: String {readOnly}
 +from(rawEmail: String): EmailAddress
}
class PasswordHash <<Value Object>> {
 -encodedValue: String {readOnly}
}
class Role <<Aggregate>> {
 -id: Long
 -name: RoleName
}
class Permission <<Value Object>> {
 -resource: String {readOnly}
 -action: String {readOnly}
}
enum RoleName {
 BUYER
 MERCHANT
}
enum AccountStatus {
 ACTIVE
 SUSPENDED
 DEACTIVATED
}
class AccountLockoutPolicy <<domain policy>> {
 -failureThreshold: Integer {readOnly}
 -lockDuration: Duration {readOnly}
 +reachesThreshold(failedAttempts: Integer): Boolean
 +lockedUntil(now: Instant): Instant
}
class SignInDecision <<Value Object>> {
 -allowed: Boolean {readOnly}
 -retryAt: Instant [0..1] {readOnly}
 -securityCheckRequired: Boolean {readOnly}
}
User "1" --> "1" EmailAddress
User "1" --> "1" PasswordHash
User "0..*" --> "1..*" Role : assigned memberships
Role "0..*" --> "0..*" Permission : granted capabilities
User ..> AccountStatus
Role ..> RoleName
User ..> AccountLockoutPolicy
User ..> SignInDecision
note bottom of User
 Hash verification and JWT issuance are application ports, not domain operations.
 Threshold failures set lockedUntil and require a security check.
 Before expiry: deny new login, do not extend the deadline on blocked requests.
 After expiry: require valid security proof before checking the password.
 A completed post-lock attempt starts a new failure window.
 Only successful password + required proof fully clears sign-in controls.
 Login lockout does not revoke an already-issued access token.
end note
note bottom of EmailAddress
 Validate syntax, trim surrounding whitespace, normalize case for identity lookup.
 Same normalization on registration/login; UNIQUE canonical email.
 This application chooses case-insensitive email identities.
end note
note bottom of PasswordHash
 Persist encoded hash only; raw password never enters domain events/resources/logs.
 HashingService handles encoding and matching outside the domain.
 Password policy and encoder parameters require explicit configuration.
end note
note bottom of Role
 Seed BUYER and MERCHANT idempotently; preserve ids and existing memberships.
 Public registration selects one supported persona, not arbitrary role/permission ids.
 MERCHANT membership does not prove RUC validity or store ownership.
 Privileged price-reports:resolve is not granted by either public persona.
 Role administration and account lifecycle workflows remain out of AV2 scope.
end note
note bottom of AccountLockoutPolicy
 Configure a positive threshold and duration; no invented numeric defaults.
 Missing policy configuration prevents successful service readiness.
 Security check verification is an application dependency, not an ACL.
end note
@enduml
